\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces On the first capture (left), 5 individuals are captured and marked with a yellow mark, from an unknown population size N. On the second capture (centre), a further 5 individuals are marked with a blue mark. Two of these also had a yellow mark, and three are new to being marked. On the third capture (right), 5 individuals are marked with a red mark. Two of these already had a yellow mark and a red mark, and one had a red mark but no yellow mark. Two are new to being marked.}}{60}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-snails-capture-mark}{{7.1}{60}{On the first capture (left), 5 individuals are captured and marked with a yellow mark, from an unknown population size N. On the second capture (centre), a further 5 individuals are marked with a blue mark. Two of these also had a yellow mark, and three are new to being marked. On the third capture (right), 5 individuals are marked with a red mark. Two of these already had a yellow mark and a red mark, and one had a red mark but no yellow mark. Two are new to being marked}{figure.caption.28}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.2}{\ignorespaces The original mark-recapture data from Jolly (1965) where the most recent previous marks on each of the individuals has been recorded over 13 catches. Note that the total released is increasingly lower than the number captured as there is a mortality risk associated with capture. For example, of the 146 individuals captured on day 2, only 143 were released.}}{61}{figure.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-jolly-mark-recapture}{{7.2}{61}{The original mark-recapture data from Jolly (1965) where the most recent previous marks on each of the individuals has been recorded over 13 catches. Note that the total released is increasingly lower than the number captured as there is a mortality risk associated with capture. For example, of the 146 individuals captured on day 2, only 143 were released}{figure.caption.29}{}}
